WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:14.010
[NARRATOR]
Two years have passed since the war
between the Navy, the Seven Warlords,

3
00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.910
and the Whitebeard Alliance,

4
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:20.050
but its repercussions are still
felt throughout the world.

5
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:24.850
This is the deserted island of Luscaina,
northwest of Amazon Lily.

6
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:28.890
[MARGARET]
Luffy!

7
00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.890
[LUFFY]
Yeah! I'm coming!

8
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.240
[LUFFY]
Time really sneaks up on you, huh?

9
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.410
Two years already.

10
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.040
[gasps]

11
00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.480
[roars]

12
00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:22.690
[LUFFY]
Hey!

13
00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:23.990
[gasps]

14
00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.560
[LUFFY]
Find someone else
to eat. She's my friend.

15
00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.000
[ALL gasp]

16
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.800
[sighs]

17
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.370
Luffy, the ship is all ready to sail.

18
00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.140
Give the word, and we'll be off.

19
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.770
[LUFFY]
Got it. Thanks.

20
00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:43.780
[HANCOCK laughs]

21
00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:44.980
I should've known.

22
00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.940
He's the boss of the whole island now.

23
00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.600
[LUFFY]
Yeah, it's kind of a shame.

24
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.270
I was planning on eating these guys,

25
00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.710
but since we're friends now,
that would be weird, huh?

26
00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.780
They still look pretty yummy, though.

27
00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.930
Don't you worry about food.

28
00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.190
I have all of your favorites
ready and waiting on the ship.

29
00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.320
Since I'm so thoughtful,
I wouldn't blame you

30
00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:08.020
if you wanted to get
married right away.

31
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.060
[LUFFY]
I'll pass on the marriage,
but thanks for the food.

32
00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.660
Ah! Cold as ever, and yet
my heart is on fire!

33
00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.100
[SANDERSONIA]
I heard that Rayleigh left
a whole six months ago.

34
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.370
I assume he's waiting for
you back on Sabaody now.

35
00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.510
[LUFFY]
Yeah, I learned the basics
a little ahead of schedule.

36
00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:28.110
All that's left is to say bye
to my friends here, I guess.

37
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.820
[LUFFY]
So long, you guys.

38
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.520
Time to go!

39
00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:33.780
<b>Ten-Odd Days Later at a Bar</b>

40
00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:39.800
<b>Two Years Later</b>

41
00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.750
[BARTENDER A]
Did you hear? They relocated Navy HQ.

42
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.380
[NAMI]
Oh? Did they now?

43
00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:51.290
Yeah. They traded locations
with a branch called G1.

44
00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.050
That moved them to the
other side of the Red Line.

45
00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:58.000
Their new fleet admiral's a lot
more cocky than Sengoku was.

46
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.810
Moved right into the Four
Emperor's territory.

47
00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.080
He's not afraid to stare
down the toughest pirates

48
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.040
On the upside, that keeps them out
of our business, but on the downside,

49
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.800
we've got a lot more
criminals running around

50
00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.150
and nobody to stop them
if things get ugly.

51
00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:13.320
Oh.

52
00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:17.560
It did seem like there were an awful
lot of thugs compared to two years ago.

53
00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.660
[GOSSIPING MAN A]
Hey, did you catch this?

54
00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.230
[GOSSIPING MAN B]
Yeah, it's a shocker, huh?

55
00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.340
I had to do a double take,

56
00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.740
but it looks like the Straw
Hats are back after all.

57
00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:27.540
I never heard word of them
dying or anything,

58
00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.210
but two years is a long time for
anyone to just disappear like that.

59
00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.180
<b>URGENT:
 CREW NEEDED</b>

60
00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.460
[GOSSIPING MAN A]
Either way, looks like they're
recruiting some new members.

61
00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:35.860
[GOSSIPING MAN C]
This is a good place for it.

62
00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:39.430
If you made it here, that means you
survived the first half of the Grand Line,

63
00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.460
and those guys keep pouring in.

64
00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:42.820
[GOSSIPING MAN B]
His crew's pretty small.

65
00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:46.120
Makes sense that he'd wanna pick up some
more before heading to the New World.

66
00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.060
That sounds like fun to me!

67
00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.660
I'd make a great Straw Hat, right?

68
00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.760
[GOSSIPING MAN B]
Fat chance.

69
00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.100
There's guys with 100 million berry
bounties all over the place here.

70
00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.800
[GOSSIPING MAN C]
Ha. What would
they want with a chump like you?

71
00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:57.800
[GOSSIPING MAN B laughs]

72
00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.920
[GOSSIPING MAN A]
That's cruel, man.

73
00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:03.010
<b>Sabaody Park, Grove 33</b>

74
00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:01.270
[GOSSIPING MAN A gasps]

75
00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:06.180
<b>The Sabao Dome, a Concert Hall</b>

76
00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.250
There's gotta be something you can do!

77
00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.480
Like what? We're sold out!

78
00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:14.450
This is the Soul King World Tour!

79
00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:18.860
You can't waltz up and buy tickets
when the show is about to start!

80
00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.280
This is the final concert
of the tour, too!

81
00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.610
Can't you hear 'em?
The crowd is ready to rock!

82
00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.610
[SOUL KING FANS cheering]

83
00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.930
Hey, manager!

84
00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:35.030
Let's make this the greatest
show of my afterlife!

85
00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.220
[LONGARM BOSS]
Well, of course! Of course!

86
00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:38.320
Now would be the time!

87
00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.690
Your TDs are at the
height of their sales.

88
00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:43.160
In fact, we just broke a million!

89
00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.300
You certainly earned your
title as the King of Soul.

90
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.230
Just listen to those fans
chanting your name!

91
00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.600
[BROOK]
I can dig it, boss man.

92
00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.770
But one thing before the concert.

93
00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.480
I got somethin' heavy to lay on ya.

94
00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.310
I'm all ears, friend.

95
00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:10.090
[SOUL KING FANS cheering]

96
00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.830
Come on, baby!

97
00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.750
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

98
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.050
I love you down to my...

99
00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:18.420
– Bone!
– Bone!

100
00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.290
Bone!

101
00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.390
– Bone!
– Bone!

102
00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:21.360
Bone!

103
00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.430
– Bone!
– Bone!

104
00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:22.920
Bone!

105
00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:23.890
Bone!

106
00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:25.860
Bone! Bone! Bone!

107
00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.330
Bone!

108
00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:41.460
[LONGARM BOSS]
I'm gonna wring his sorry neck bone!

109
00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.420
How selfish can he be?

110
00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:45.960
Hey! Grab me a transponder snail!

111
00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:49.840
I'm not gonna let you
walk all over me, Brook!

112
00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:13.850
Women! Real women!

113
00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:17.020
No stubble! No hairy
legs! No giant chins!

114
00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:21.090
Just honest to goodness
beautiful girls!

115
00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:23.290
How I've longed for your
delicate features.

116
00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:24.830
Your soft skin.

117
00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:27.430
To hear the intoxicating words
resting on your sweet lips!

118
00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.390
Viva Sabaody!

119
00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:31.590
I need lady!

120
00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.890
[laughing]

121
00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.970
[PINK-STRIPED QUEEN]
Sanji, dear!

122
00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:36.970
It looks like this is farewell.

123
00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:40.410
I hate to part, but we'll
meet again someday.

124
00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:42.870
I hope not!

125
00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:42.580
[SANJI]
Uh!

126
00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.890
Thanks for the ride and say
hi to Iva, but go away!

127
00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.050
What's up, ladies?

128
00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:51.530
I'm fresh outta hell and
lookin' for a good time!

129
00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:56.260
Like they say, if a boy picks on a girl,
that means he has a crush on her.

130
00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.630
Oh, I know. Happens to me all the time.

131
00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.060
Love is patient, Sanji!

132
00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.960
We'll wait! We know you'll come back!

133
00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:06.470
I'm on my way, Nami-swan!
Robin, my love!

134
00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:07.670
[gunshot]

135
00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:14.540
[MAN]
What's the matter, can't read?

136
00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.250
Or are you just stupid?

137
00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:20.650
I know preschoolers with
higher bounties than that.

138
00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:30.090
<b>Captain Monkey D. Luffy
"Straw Hat Pirates"</b>

139
00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:22.860
How 'bout you check that poster again.

140
00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:26.530
If your bounty is under 70
million, then we don't want you.

141
00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:30.730
So why don't you take your weak
ass back to pirate daycare?

142
00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:34.600
If that's all you're worth, it's
a wonder you made it this far.

143
00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.500
Bastard!

144
00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:38.880
[FAKE LUFFY]
Now scram.

145
00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:41.010
I'm the son of Dragon
the Revolutionary!

146
00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.830
I ain't got time for this!

147
00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:45.370
<b>Navigator Nami</b>

148
00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:46.060
[chuckles]

149
00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:50.510
<b>Shipwright Franky</b>

150
00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:48.460
We're the chosen ones, boyo.

151
00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.830
No chumps are gonna run with this crew.

152
00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:56.180
<b>Marksman Sogeking</b>

153
00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.970
We're in a league of our own!

154
00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:56.970
If you can't get with us,
you better get the hell out of our way!

155
00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.840
Too late.

156
00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:01.640
[gunshot]

157
00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:07.350
That's rough. Straw Hat is fierce.

158
00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:10.020
'Course he is. He's a legend.

159
00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:14.790
What's the count, Franky?
How many recruits we got?

160
00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:16.790
[FAKE FRANKY]
'Bout a hundred last time I checked.

161
00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:20.890
Three whole crews joined up
along with ten guys running solo.

162
00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.710
They've got some nice bounties, too.

163
00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.680
[chuckles]

164
00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:24.180
I know two of 'em.

165
00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.940
Pair of high-profile rookies
joined at the same time.

166
00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.680
"Wet-Haired" Caribou
and "Blood Splatter" Coribou.

167
00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:35.510
They love killin' Marines.

168
00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:39.780
Brothers and captains worth
210 million and 190 million.

169
00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:43.750
Ha! Now, they answer to us!

170
00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:45.990
And there's more where they came from!

171
00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.760
Hey! Bring another round!

172
00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:49.630
Uh! Yes, sir!

173
00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:51.660
Better make it quick.

174
00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:57.070
Ah. I see you sittin'
alone over there, missy.

175
00:10:57.070 --> 00:11:00.480
If you wanna have a good time,
why don't you party with us?

176
00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.380
She's a real looker, ain't she?

177
00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:05.210
[FAKE LUFFY laughing]

178
00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.800
I'll pass. I'm here
waiting for a friend.

179
00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:15.740
This is about to get ugly.

180
00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:18.410
Listen, I would not turn that man down.

181
00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.780
You realize that's Straw
Hat Luffy, right?

182
00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.510
Yeah, the same Straw Hat
that burst into Marineford

183
00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:26.060
and went head to head
with the Navy Admirals.

184
00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.030
He's nuts.

185
00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:28.780
[FAKE USOPP laughs]

186
00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.010
Waitin' for a friend?

187
00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:32.350
Captain Luffy is a star, baby.

188
00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:35.560
Your "friend" would probably
piss his pants if he saw him.

189
00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:38.060
Come drink with some real men.

190
00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:43.000
I'm only going to say this once.

191
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.170
You can take your offer and shove it,
'cause I'm way out of your league.

192
00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.310
What?

193
00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.910
You understand?

194
00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:57.080
Mister... whoever you are.

195
00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:03.370
You don't know me? [BARTENDER A gasps]

196
00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.340
I'm Straw Hat Luffy, you wench!

197
00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:10.780
Hey, come on! Say you're sorry! Hurry!

198
00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:08.220
Ah!

199
00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:20.230
Nobody disrespects me!

200
00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:26.890
Let me handle this.

201
00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:31.260
Har-har. You think you're
real cute, don't you?

202
00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.340
I'll make this super simple, okay?

203
00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:40.330
Either you come drink with
Captain Luffy, or you die.

204
00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:41.330
[FAKE NAMI giggles]

205
00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.800
For your info, I have a bounty, myself.

206
00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.660
I'm the Straw Hat's navigator, Nami.

207
00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.530
You scared yet?

208
00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:51.300
Special Attack... Green Star...

209
00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.110
"Devil"!

210
00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:58.480
[FAKE NAMI screaming]

211
00:12:58.480 --> 00:12:59.680
Huh?

212
00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:04.360
Whoa. What the hell?

213
00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.690
[FAKE NAMI]
Captain! Save me!

214
00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:10.470
[FAKE LUFFY]
Save yourself! Get away from me!

215
00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:13.650
A giant plant? Where'd that come from?

216
00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:16.990
Hey there, beautiful.
Can I buy ya a drink?

217
00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:18.020
[NAMI gasps]

218
00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:21.850
[chuckles]

219
00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:24.020
Ah!

220
00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:26.760
Look at you! Those
muscles! And that hair!

221
00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:29.390
You tough guy! You
look great! I missed you!

222
00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:32.900
[USOPP]
Uh, thanks. Uh, your,
uh, hair looks nice, too.

223
00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:34.370
[chuckles]

224
00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.740
That hot girl was waiting
for that pencil-nosed geek?

225
00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:38.380
What does he have that we don't?

226
00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.740
New special move, huh?

227
00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:41.210
[USOPP chuckles]

228
00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.550
[USOPP]
Yeah, they come from
seeds called "pop greens."

229
00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:47.940
Needless to say, I wasn't just sitting
around on my tail these past two years.

230
00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:49.840
It's a new me!

231
00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.510
I'm not part of the "weakling trio"

232
00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.550
with you and Chopper anymore.

233
00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:55.580
That means no more running and hiding.

234
00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:57.580
I'm a real warrior now!

235
00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:01.420
Uh. Hey, dude? If you did
this, could you undo it?

236
00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:04.490
What the...?! Sniper King?! But how?

237
00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:06.790
Usopp, forget about them!

238
00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:09.230
Let's get outta here. There's
something we need to talk about.

239
00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:10.860
You stop right there!

240
00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.570
– Luffy?
[NAMI]
– Ignore him!

241
00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:14.570
Ma'am, you haven't paid your tab yet!

242
00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:15.600
[USOPP]
Keep the change!

243
00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.460
Crap! They're makin' fools of us!

244
00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.530
Gun 'em down now!

245
00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:24.840
Son of a...

246
00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.040
Huh?

247
00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:29.210
Um, guys? What are those
weird bubble things?

248
00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:32.410
[popping]

249
00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:39.240
[FAKE LUFFY]
I have a feelin'
this ain't gonna be pretty.

250
00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:45.910
[thunder rumbles]

251
00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:51.500
[WOMAN A screaming]

252
00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.600
What the hell's going on here?

253
00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:56.600
Yeah, so I picked up some
new special moves myself.

254
00:14:56.600 --> 00:15:00.210
You show off! Can't you
let me be cool for once?

255
00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:18.420
[MAN C gasps]

256
00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.800
[FAKE FRANKY coughs]

257
00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.830
Who do they think they are?

258
00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:32.440
Hunt those bastards down
and murder 'em.

259
00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:37.520
<b>Marineford
(Former Navy HQ)</b>

260
00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:35.810
[MARINE A]
I have a report, sir!

261
00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.040
From Sabaody Archipelago!

262
00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.710
What? You say the Straw Hats are back?

263
00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.410
Yes, sir!

264
00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:45.380
Word is that they're recruiting new crew
members before they head to the New World.

265
00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.380
Had a feeling Straw
Hat was still alive.

266
00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:50.940
Inform Headquarters
of this immediately.

267
00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.550
Send in as many backup
units as we can spare

268
00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:56.210
and begin a search of
the entire archipelago.

269
00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:57.450
[BOTH]
– Sir!
– Sir!

270
00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.570
I think I shook them off.

271
00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:26.360
<b>URGENT: 
CREW NEEDED</b>

272
00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:27.950
[ROBIN]
Brook is holding a concert and the Straw
Hats are looking for new recruits?

273
00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:30.580
Goodness, I've been gone for too long.

274
00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:35.510
[ROBIN]
"Soul King" does have
a nice ring to it, though.

275
00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:40.620
<b>Shakky's Rip-off Bar, Grove 13</b>

276
00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:36.650
[SANJI]
You're kidding me.

277
00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:40.920
You're saying the swordsman who barely
knows left from right got here first?

278
00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.220
Well, whaddaya know?

279
00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:45.160
Maybe he learned how to read
a map while he was training.

280
00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:49.170
After him came Franky, about ten days
ago now, but he headed back out to go see

281
00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:51.000
if your ship was doing all right.

282
00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.240
I hope that means the
Sunny is in good shape.

283
00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.710
[RAYLEIGH]
Of course. There
isn't a single scratch on it.

284
00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:57.670
We finished the coating, too.

285
00:16:57.670 --> 00:16:58.780
[SANJI]
That's good to hear.

286
00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:01.250
Just make sure you give
credit where credit's due.

287
00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:04.190
Even if he don't, there's no
shame in a wound of honor.

288
00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:07.260
[FISH RIDERS]
– It's time for some R'n'R!
– It's time for some R'n'R!

289
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:10.130
Who knew you'd be so
dedicated to the cause?

290
00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.140
Your stubbornness came in handy.

291
00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:14.610
Y'mean my looks?

292
00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:15.940
[DUVAL laughs]

293
00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:18.250
Don't mention it.
I owed you one anyway!

294
00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.290
Come rain or shine, it changed nothin'.

295
00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:23.490
Dangerous pirates from all
over came to take that ship.

296
00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:26.880
Didn't matter how bad I was hurt,
I defended it day after day.

297
00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.450
'Cause I knew all these
bruises would be worth it!

298
00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:31.620
[BOTH]
– You're so amazing, sir!
– You're so amazing, sir!

299
00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.180
Pirates messed you up? Come on.

300
00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:34.990
What's the real story here, Duval?

301
00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.220
Don't be impatient.

302
00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.490
I'm tryin' to build up the
suspense here, y'know?

303
00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:39.720
Y'see...

304
00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:41.890
[SHAKKY]
The third member of
your crew to arrive was Nami.

305
00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:44.360
Nami!

306
00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:46.860
That's great! Is she still here?

307
00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:49.430
She decided to kill time by
getting some shopping done.

308
00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:51.640
C'mon, don'tcha wanna hear
the rest of I story?

309
00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:55.210
Nami's shopping. Nami's
shopping. Nami's shopping...

310
00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:59.220
The fourth one to arrive was Usopp
three days ago, who also went into town

311
00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.920
Followed by Chopper,
who showed up yesterday.

312
00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:03.020
Brook's made it, too.

313
00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:05.560
He's putting on a concert
for the islanders today.

314
00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.880
[SANJI]
No way.

315
00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:10.280
You're the last to stop by,
which makes seven in total.

316
00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:11.880
Not that I expected any less,

317
00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:15.450
but almost the entire crew has
made it back in good time.

318
00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.790
[RAYLEIGH]
That's right. Only
Nico Robin and Luffy remain.

319
00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:21.360
Getting to this island in the
first place is a difficult task

320
00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:23.230
for any crew to accomplish.

321
00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:25.830
And yet, you've made
it twice. What can I say?

322
00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.460
You must be eager to
see each other again.

323
00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.690
Yeah.

324
00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:33.280
And by the way, I still can't believe
you trained Luffy while we were gone.

325
00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:36.090
He must be crazy strong now.

326
00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:38.230
He's been on his own
these last six months.

327
00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:40.830
I can't wait to see how his
skills have developed.

328
00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:43.900
[SANJI]
Now that you... mention it.

329
00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:47.710
I can't wait to see how Nami's developed,
if you know what I'm sayin'!

330
00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:49.310
[RAYLEIGH]
I should've expected that.

331
00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:56.450
[CHOPPER]
Hey, guys! What's the matter?

332
00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.920
C'mon, talk to me!

333
00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:01.820
I thought you'd be more excited
to see me, but you're acting weird!

334
00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:05.590
From the looks of things, you've all
changed a lot over these last two years.

335
00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:09.060
But, I mean, we're still friends,
so why are you ignoring me?

336
00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:11.220
Yo, man. It's not leaving.

337
00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:14.290
Oh, you must be shy 'cause of
how much I've changed, too!

338
00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:18.280
And if you ask me, that furball knows
a little bit too much about us "Straw Hats,"

339
00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:19.590
if you know what I mean.

340
00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:22.170
Yeah, I do, and ya gotta
wonder why that is.

341
00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:24.500
Maybe we can find the answer here.

342
00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:25.250
<b>Zoro, Sanji, Robin & Chopper
"Straw Hat Pirates"</b>

343
00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.970
[FAKE ZORO]
Uh! No, it can't be!

344
00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:29.860
[CHOPPER]
Huh?

345
00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:31.900
That's the real deal
cotton-candy-lovin'

346
00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.600
Tony Tony Chopper!

347
00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:35.770
The pet's comin' home!

348
00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:39.640
So we all look a little different
than we used to, who cares?

349
00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.930
He must've been abandoned
on this island when they died

350
00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:44.700
and has been living
in the wild ever since.

351
00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.330
And now he's following us around

352
00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:49.260
because he thinks his masters
have finally come back for him.

353
00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:52.190
We should ditch the mutt
and take him instead.

354
00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:56.500
If we have their real pet, no one will
ever doubt that we're the Straw Hats again!

355
00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.060
Sounds good. What's he eat?

356
00:19:58.060 --> 00:19:59.300
[FAKE SANJI]
Probably cotton candy.

357
00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.540
We ain't got none o' that!

358
00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.810
[FAKE CHOPPER grunting]

359
00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:05.340
[FAKE ROBIN]
Get! We don't need you no more!

360
00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:08.210
[gasps]

361
00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:10.880
[FAKE ROBIN]
C'mere, boy, ya hungry?

362
00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:13.540
[roars]

363
00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.350
Yum. Right?

364
00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:17.050
[CHOPPER]
You're kinda freaking me out!

365
00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:18.720
[BLACK SUIT MAN A]
Now!

366
00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:19.720
[FAKE ROBIN]
Huh?

367
00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:22.620
[CHOPPER]
Robin!

368
00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.790
Hey! Stop! Come back!

369
00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:25.960
Who were those creeps?

370
00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:28.490
Oh, no! This is a real emergency!

371
00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.310
What're we gonna do now?

372
00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:32.750
I guess we should tell
Captain Luffy, right?

373
00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.870
Maybe he knows how to handle this mess.

374
00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:37.830
Wait! I didn't know Luffy was
back on the island already!

375
00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.570
You're right. And he'll
have new recruits by now.

376
00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:41.590
That's great!

377
00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.970
With the extra might,
we'll save Robin for sure!

378
00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.480
Let's go get our friend back!

379
00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:46.640
[BOTH]
– Huh?
– Huh?

380
00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:48.310
[BOTH chuckle]

381
00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:49.810
[BLACK SUIT MAN A]
Calling from Sabaody!

382
00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.350
We've secured Nico Robin!

383
00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.990
We've also caught some fox thing
that won't stop biting her head.

384
00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:57.370
It's been a while.

385
00:20:57.370 --> 00:20:59.980
Surely the others have
made it back by now.

386
00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:07.520
Oh! Hey! Are you all right? Hey!

387
00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:10.960
Why did he do that? He just
shot her out of the blue!

388
00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.390
[WOMAN B]
That's awful!

389
00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:14.530
Come on, we'll get a doctor.

390
00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:16.570
You! What is wrong with you?

391
00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:19.170
She didn't do a damn
thing to deserve that!

392
00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:21.340
[FAKE LUFFY]
Ugh. I thought you were someone else.

393
00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:24.400
I said sorry. So, here's the deal.

394
00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:28.270
I'm lookin' for some punks who
crossed me and made a run for it.

395
00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:31.440
A red-haired woman and
a guy with a long nose.

396
00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:34.600
So you just shot her?
That's normal for you?

397
00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:37.690
This won't end well.
Straw Hat's a monster.

398
00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:40.020
Eh? You wanna fight about it?

399
00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:42.190
'Cause I got plenty more bullets.

400
00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:46.530
Your choice, pal.

401
00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.460
[MAN I screams]

402
00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:53.330
Don't blame me. Blame your nose!

403
00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:56.400
Hey. We'll get some help! Stay with me!

404
00:21:56.400 --> 00:22:00.170
Find those punks now,
or I'll shoot you, too!

405
00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:03.920
We got a reputation to uphold here!

406
00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:06.490
We gotta show this place who's boss!

407
00:22:20.630 --> 00:22:21.330
[BOTH gasp]

408
00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:22.300
[gasps]

409
00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:26.270
[LUFFY]
Uh?

410
00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:28.340
Oops. Didn't see ya there.

411
00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:32.210
Sorry 'bout that. See ya.

412
00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:33.840
That's guy's insane!

413
00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:37.380
Either that, or he doesn't
know who Straw Hat is.

414
00:22:37.380 --> 00:22:39.550
He's a dead man either way!

415
00:22:41.480 --> 00:22:43.350
Get back here!

416
00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:03.750
[HANCOCK]
There in the distance
is Sabaody Archipelago.

417
00:23:03.750 --> 00:23:07.320
Forgive me, Luffy, but we will
have to say our goodbyes here.

418
00:23:07.320 --> 00:23:11.530
We cannot let anyone discover
the nature of our relationship.

419
00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:12.280
[LUFFY]
Uh-huh.

420
00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:14.130
[HANCOCK]
I've prepared...

421
00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:16.190
a disguise for you.

422
00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:17.850
[LUFFY]
Ha-ha. Are you kidding?

423
00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:19.320
I can't pull that look off!

424
00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:23.190
Perhaps. But I would still feel
more at ease if you took it.

425
00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:24.930
[LUFFY]
All right.

426
00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:26.630
[HANCOCK]
You must be careful.

427
00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.300
Keep your face hidden at all times.

428
00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:33.440
The world may believe you've
been dead these last two years,

429
00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:37.580
but that won't stop anyone from recognizing
you the first time you get into trouble.

430
00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:41.620
So if you ever want to set sail again,
you'll take my advice to heart.

431
00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:43.290
[LUFFY]
Thanks. I'll try.

432
00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:44.290
You're welcome.

433
00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:46.990
Now, for supplies,
I've loaded your backpack

434
00:23:46.990 --> 00:23:51.010
with 50 changes of clothes, 1,000
lunches, handkerchiefs, and tissues.

435
00:23:51.010 --> 00:23:54.620
You'll also find three years' worth
of water, snacks, and bug bite ointment.

436
00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:57.220
There's also five years' worth
of towels, toothbrushes,

437
00:23:57.220 --> 00:23:59.360
plenty of soaps, hand creams,
and lots of silverware.

438
00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:01.190
That is entirely too much!

439
00:24:01.190 --> 00:24:02.760
[HANCOCK giggles]

440
00:24:04.300 --> 00:24:06.810
Well, I hope you can
find all your friends.

441
00:24:06.810 --> 00:24:09.640
[LUFFY]
Thanks again for getting
me here and all the other stuff.

442
00:24:09.060 --> 00:24:09.890
[MARGARET chuckles]

443
00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:11.590
We were more than happy to help you.

444
00:24:12.250 --> 00:24:14.580
Your most difficult trials
may still be ahead of you.

445
00:24:14.580 --> 00:24:16.490
I hear that Sabaody has
become a den of crime.

446
00:24:16.490 --> 00:24:17.190
[NYON]
Mh-hm.

447
00:24:17.190 --> 00:24:19.330
And because of that, the Navy
has been keeping a tight watch

448
00:24:20.330 --> 00:24:22.670
over the goings-on there
as of late, my boy.

449
00:24:22.670 --> 00:24:24.940
So be sure to take extra care!

450
00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:25.940
[LUFFY]
Right.

451
00:24:25.940 --> 00:24:29.950
[HANCOCK]
If you ever need assistance, the full
force of the Kuja Pirates will come rushing

452
00:24:29.950 --> 00:24:32.080
to your aide at a moment's notice.

453
00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:34.450
Please, don't hesitate to call on us.

454
00:24:36.120 --> 00:24:38.990
Also, would you be willing
to do me a favor?

455
00:24:38.990 --> 00:24:41.430
Yeah, maybe. Long as
it's not getting married.

456
00:24:41.430 --> 00:24:43.060
No, no.

457
00:24:43.060 --> 00:24:48.000
All I ask is that, when you leave,
you do so without saying "farewell."

458
00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:49.000
That all?

459
00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:51.500
I've never said that to
anyone before, so sure!

460
00:24:51.500 --> 00:24:53.430
Besides, I wanna see you again!

461
00:24:53.430 --> 00:24:54.570
[HANCOCK squeals]

462
00:24:54.570 --> 00:24:58.070
[chuckles]

463
00:24:58.070 --> 00:25:00.070
[LUFFY]
All right! I'm outta here!

464
00:25:00.070 --> 00:25:02.620
[AMAZONS bidding adieu]

465
00:25:02.620 --> 00:25:04.690
You take care!

466
00:25:04.690 --> 00:25:05.890
[HANCOCK]
Oh, my.

467
00:25:05.890 --> 00:25:07.960
He wants to see me again.

468
00:25:07.960 --> 00:25:11.900
That's practically a... a proposal!

469
00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:13.680
No, it's not!

470
00:25:16.330 --> 00:25:19.600
Hancock told me I gotta stay
outta trouble and lay low.

471
00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:21.310
I don't wanna fight this guy.

472
00:25:21.310 --> 00:25:25.480
Hey, dummy. Did you
run into me on purpose?

473
00:25:25.480 --> 00:25:28.620
[MAN AA]
Oh, no. He's gonna kill that poor guy!

474
00:26:07.190 --> 00:26:08.690
Hi, Sunny.

475
00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:17.770
[ROBIN]
Sorry to keep you waiting.

476
00:26:17.770 --> 00:26:19.500
I hope you weren't lonely.

477
00:26:21.370 --> 00:26:24.210
You're as lovely as ever.

478
00:26:24.210 --> 00:26:25.540
[FRANKY]
Huh?

479
00:26:25.540 --> 00:26:28.710
[FRANKY screams]

480
00:26:28.710 --> 00:26:29.780
[gasps]

481
00:26:29.780 --> 00:26:32.320
[FRANKY]
Now who is that gorgeous lady?

482
00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:34.520
It's Robin, of course!

483
00:26:34.520 --> 00:26:37.050
Our super archaeologist!

484
00:26:42.330 --> 00:26:44.470
Boy, did I miss you!

485
00:27:03.880 --> 00:27:06.350
[chuckles]
You haven't
changed a bit, Franky!

486
00:27:06.350 --> 00:27:09.190
[FRANKY]
Is that a joke,
sister? I'm a brand new man!

487
00:27:09.190 --> 00:27:10.720
No, I'm more than a man!

488
00:27:10.720 --> 00:27:13.430
I'm the stuff dreams are made of!

489
00:27:13.430 --> 00:27:16.370
Gaze upon this fantastic
transformation,

490
00:27:16.370 --> 00:27:19.180
the likes of which this
world has never seen!

491
00:27:19.180 --> 00:27:24.680
Yeah, baby! I'm beyond
human comprehension!

492
00:27:24.680 --> 00:27:25.880
Fair enough.

493
00:27:25.880 --> 00:27:28.850
Though I might argue that you've been
that way for quite some time now.

494
00:27:28.850 --> 00:27:32.500
[FRANKY]
Huh? So, I'm not just
a freak, I'm a super freak?

495
00:27:32.500 --> 00:27:35.200
Ha! You're gonna make me blush!

496
00:27:43.130 --> 00:27:46.400
This is the coating, I take it?

497
00:27:46.400 --> 00:27:48.640
Hah. It's like jelly.

498
00:27:48.640 --> 00:27:49.540
Yep!

499
00:27:49.540 --> 00:27:53.140
Took a little longer than we expected,
but Rayleigh did his part!

500
00:27:53.140 --> 00:27:55.140
Bottom of the sea, here we come!

501
00:27:55.140 --> 00:27:57.120
After everyone gets back, of course.

502
00:27:57.120 --> 00:27:59.960
Speaking of which,
I saw Rayleigh at the bar.

503
00:27:59.960 --> 00:28:02.190
[FRANKY]
Oh, yeah? What number were you?

504
00:28:02.190 --> 00:28:03.660
Who're we missin'?

505
00:28:03.660 --> 00:28:05.430
I was number eight.

506
00:28:05.430 --> 00:28:07.760
So, the only one left is him.

507
00:28:07.760 --> 00:28:08.870
Luffy.

508
00:28:08.870 --> 00:28:11.670
Well, I'm sure our captain'll
show up soon enough.

509
00:28:11.670 --> 00:28:14.000
The ship's ready whenever he is.

510
00:28:16.610 --> 00:28:18.610
New weapon's ready, too.

511
00:28:18.610 --> 00:28:20.750
[laughs]

512
00:28:20.750 --> 00:28:22.520
That sounds just splendid.

513
00:28:22.520 --> 00:28:25.200
By the way, where is
everyone else? Busy?

514
00:28:25.200 --> 00:28:27.820
Usopp and Sanji stopped
by here earlier.

515
00:28:27.820 --> 00:28:30.230
Usopp's pickin' up some
fuel for the trip.

516
00:28:30.230 --> 00:28:32.610
Sanji's getting groceries, of course.

517
00:28:32.610 --> 00:28:36.920
I see. I ran into something
interesting on the way over.

518
00:28:36.920 --> 00:28:38.720
Have you seen these?

519
00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:39.420
[FRANKY]
Huh?

520
00:28:39.420 --> 00:28:40.950
It's for a concert today.

521
00:28:41.750 --> 00:28:43.860
He's calling himself "Soul King."

522
00:28:43.860 --> 00:28:46.260
Yeah, there's a story behind that.

523
00:28:46.260 --> 00:28:47.530
He's big news now.

524
00:28:47.530 --> 00:28:51.580
They're sellin' his TDs
all over the place.

525
00:28:51.580 --> 00:28:54.180
He's left the darkness far behind.

526
00:28:51.600 --> 00:28:53.030
Heh.

527
00:28:55.700 --> 00:28:56.660
Huh?

528
00:28:56.660 --> 00:29:00.330
[FRANKY]
He rose up from those foggy seas
and now he's a shining star.

529
00:29:00.330 --> 00:29:04.170
His fans raise his name to the heavens,
if you'll pardon my poetry.

530
00:29:07.890 --> 00:29:10.690
[FRANKY]
He didn't say
anything about this to me,

531
00:29:13.010 --> 00:29:16.350
but he's makin' a lot of
people happy with his music.

532
00:29:16.350 --> 00:29:19.000
He might not wanna be a pirate anymore.

533
00:29:16.570 --> 00:29:20.580
<b>The Sabao Dome, Grove 33</b>

534
00:29:19.620 --> 00:29:20.820
[SOUL KING FANS cheering]

535
00:29:21.280 --> 00:29:25.580
[BROOK]
♪ It's no mystery.
♪ Just rock with me.

536
00:29:26.350 --> 00:29:29.180
♪ And you'll see why I'm the king! ♪

537
00:29:31.420 --> 00:29:39.390
♪ Thin is in when you're a skeleton ♪
♪ 'cause calcium is all that you need! ♪

538
00:29:35.760 --> 00:29:39.390
[BACKING VOCALS]
– ♪ Calcium is all that you need! ♪
– ♪ Calcium is all that you need! ♪

539
00:29:39.390 --> 00:29:43.800
[BROOK]
♪ So, ditch that fat and protein ♪
♪ make your body mean and lean. ♪

540
00:29:43.800 --> 00:29:46.370
♪ Got milk! Got milk!

541
00:29:46.370 --> 00:29:54.340
♪ My bones are rockin' rollin', ♪
♪ soul is flowin' out of my head! ♪

542
00:29:58.230 --> 00:30:00.670
So whaddaya gotta say for yourself?

543
00:30:00.670 --> 00:30:05.000
Ya can't tell me you didn't know
who I was when ya crashed in ta me.

544
00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:06.440
Why do it?

545
00:30:06.440 --> 00:30:08.910
Were you just tryin' to
make a fool outta me?

546
00:30:08.910 --> 00:30:13.080
'Cause if so, I don't like
bein' shown up in public.

547
00:30:13.080 --> 00:30:18.380
After all, I have a reputation and
a 400 million berry bounty to uphold.

548
00:30:18.380 --> 00:30:21.620
But you can make it up
to me... by kneeling.

549
00:30:21.620 --> 00:30:24.540
Beg for your life and
I might feel generous.

550
00:30:31.080 --> 00:30:33.450
Yo! Fisherman, you in?

551
00:30:33.450 --> 00:30:36.020
Lookin' for some good
stock at a low price.

552
00:30:36.020 --> 00:30:37.620
Huh? This the place?

553
00:30:37.620 --> 00:30:39.490
[OLD FISHERMAN A whimpering]

554
00:30:39.490 --> 00:30:40.430
[SANJI]
Hm?

555
00:30:40.430 --> 00:30:42.260
Hey, you run this shack?

556
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:45.030
What's the matter?

557
00:30:45.030 --> 00:30:47.300
It's something awful!

558
00:30:47.300 --> 00:30:49.440
That green-haired man's gone!

559
00:30:49.440 --> 00:30:52.170
Aw, crap. All right, old man, spill it.

560
00:30:52.170 --> 00:30:54.670
I can't believe this
has happened to me!

561
00:30:54.670 --> 00:30:57.780
Well, y'see, uh...

562
00:30:57.780 --> 00:31:00.350
[ZORO]
Hey, gramps. I was
lookin' to do some fishing.

563
00:31:00.350 --> 00:31:00.850
Huh?

564
00:31:00.850 --> 00:31:01.950
No offense, young man,

565
00:31:02.660 --> 00:31:06.210
but I wouldn't exactly peg
you as the fishing type.

566
00:31:06.210 --> 00:31:07.800
[ZORO]
Normally you'd be right.

567
00:31:07.800 --> 00:31:10.140
I'm supposed to be meeting
some friends on this island,

568
00:31:10.140 --> 00:31:13.620
but they haven't made it yet,
so I'm bored outta my skull.

569
00:31:13.620 --> 00:31:17.220
So I need something to keep
me entertained while I wait.

570
00:31:17.220 --> 00:31:19.250
You think you can help me out, or not?

571
00:31:19.250 --> 00:31:21.840
Sure. I'll finish getting
everything we need ready,

572
00:31:21.840 --> 00:31:24.180
and then meet you on my
boat right over there.

573
00:31:25.540 --> 00:31:27.830
And that's all I said to him.

574
00:31:27.830 --> 00:31:31.500
To be clear, did this guy have
three swords and a belly warmer?

575
00:31:31.500 --> 00:31:34.690
Yes, he did! And he had a
deep scar on his eye, too!

576
00:31:34.690 --> 00:31:35.990
How'd ya know?

577
00:31:35.990 --> 00:31:38.360
Scar's new.

578
00:31:38.360 --> 00:31:39.660
Is this him?

579
00:31:39.660 --> 00:31:40.760
Yeah!

580
00:31:40.760 --> 00:31:42.490
He said he'd been waiting
on some friends to show.

581
00:31:42.490 --> 00:31:43.660
That must be you.

582
00:31:43.660 --> 00:31:46.130
[SANJI]
Well, I wouldn't go that far.

583
00:31:46.130 --> 00:31:48.630
Y'see, I told him to
wait on my fishing boat

584
00:31:48.630 --> 00:31:51.300
while I was getting ready, and
I pointed right at the thing,

585
00:31:51.300 --> 00:31:54.370
but when I came outside,
he'd made a huge mistake!

586
00:31:54.370 --> 00:31:57.030
No! Young man!

587
00:31:57.030 --> 00:32:00.360
You've got it wrong!
You're on a pirate ship!

588
00:32:00.360 --> 00:32:04.110
Now, men, it's time we set sail for
the New World we've been dreaming of!

589
00:32:04.110 --> 00:32:05.280
The wait is over!

590
00:32:05.280 --> 00:32:06.120
[PIRATES]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

591
00:32:06.120 --> 00:32:08.350
Come on, please! You have to wake up!

592
00:32:08.350 --> 00:32:10.450
You got on the wrong ship!

593
00:32:11.490 --> 00:32:17.340
[OLD FISHERMAN A]
Since they went underwater, I'd guess
there were headed to Fishman Island.

594
00:32:21.510 --> 00:32:23.010
That idiot!

595
00:32:28.570 --> 00:32:32.140
[SANJI]
Should've known him showing up
here first was too good to be true.

596
00:32:32.140 --> 00:32:34.980
Wouldn't be Zoro if he didn't
get lost somewhere.

597
00:32:34.980 --> 00:32:36.410
Aren't you worried at all?

598
00:32:36.410 --> 00:32:37.910
They might kill him on that ship!

599
00:32:37.910 --> 00:32:39.850
It's fine, don't get worked up.

600
00:32:39.850 --> 00:32:42.520
This is pretty standard fare, actually.

601
00:32:42.520 --> 00:32:45.650
Better than usual, even, since we
know where he's going for once.

602
00:32:45.650 --> 00:32:47.820
Now, would you mind selling
me some fish already?

603
00:32:47.820 --> 00:32:49.290
I don't think you understand.

604
00:32:49.290 --> 00:32:50.090
[MEN chattering]

605
00:32:49.920 --> 00:32:51.490
[MAN N]
Whoa! See that?

606
00:32:51.490 --> 00:32:54.060
[MAN II]
Look at the waves!
Somethin's coming up!

607
00:32:54.060 --> 00:32:55.130
[SANJI]
Hm?

608
00:32:57.770 --> 00:32:59.100
[MAN JJ]
But what?

609
00:32:59.100 --> 00:33:01.240
[MAN KK]
It must be huge!

610
00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:05.470
[MEN gasp]

611
00:33:10.140 --> 00:33:11.750
[MEN]
– Whoa!
– Whoa!

612
00:33:12.710 --> 00:33:14.650
[MAN LL]
That's a galleon ship!

613
00:33:14.650 --> 00:33:17.760
[MAN O]
It must've had poor coating and was
crushed under the water pressure!

614
00:33:17.760 --> 00:33:19.690
No, it has to be the work of Sea Kings!

615
00:33:19.690 --> 00:33:21.430
[MAN MM]
But it looks like
it's been cut in half.

616
00:33:21.430 --> 00:33:23.330
Like someone attacked it!

617
00:33:23.330 --> 00:33:25.690
No way! Just think for a second!

618
00:33:25.690 --> 00:33:26.830
Who in the world could do that?

619
00:33:26.830 --> 00:33:28.600
Damn you! Tell me why!

620
00:33:28.600 --> 00:33:32.600
How could you just ruin our dreams
of reaching the New World like this?

621
00:33:34.170 --> 00:33:35.780
[ZORO]
Call it a twist of fate.

622
00:33:35.780 --> 00:33:38.280
That's what brought this
plague upon your ship.

623
00:33:38.280 --> 00:33:41.380
And there's no one for you
to blame but yourselves.

624
00:33:41.380 --> 00:33:43.550
Are you kidding me?

625
00:33:43.550 --> 00:33:44.420
[MAN P]
Look!

626
00:33:44.420 --> 00:33:45.720
Who the heck is that guy?

627
00:33:45.720 --> 00:33:50.380
Oh, great. Back already...
and he's still a pain in the ass.

628
00:33:58.560 --> 00:34:03.210
That... wasn't my ride.
